    <h1>About IncenseHub</h1>
    <p><em>Last updated: 2026-10-23 · Applies to incensehub.org and data.incensehub.org</em></p>

    <p class="lead">
      IncenseHub is a research-led, English-language platform for Chinese botanical incense: its
      materials, botanicals, history, terminology, craft, and culture. It is published by
      <strong>IncenseHub</strong>. This page states who we are, what we
      publish, how we work, and — just as deliberately — what we do not claim.
    </p>

    <h2>What IncenseHub is</h2>
    <p>
      IncenseHub is a <strong>knowledge platform</strong> — an ingredient encyclopedia, technique and
      history guides, and structured open datasets — for Chinese botanical incense. The name
      IncenseHub means "lantern on the waves" — a soft glow over still water. It is the brand
      name under which the company publishes its editorial content.
    </p>
    <p>
      The platform is organized around one rule: knowledge is documented with source transparency.
      Every factual claim carries a source that resolves and supports the sentence it sits behind, or
      is labelled as traditional, editorial, or unverified.
    </p>

    <h2>What we publish</h2>
    <p>The site is organized around a few clear strands:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>An ingredient encyclopedia</strong> — source-transparent entries for the woods, resins,
        flowers, herbs, and spices used in Chinese incense, each documenting identity, processing,
        grading, and safety, with an Evidence &amp; Sources section.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Guides and reference</strong> — the history of Chinese incense, the way of incense
        (香道), the 合香 blending system, and technique guides.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Structured open datasets</strong> — on data.incensehub.org, the same entities are
        published as machine-readable Schema.org datasets (ingredients, terminology, relationships,
        comparisons, materials, forms, techniques, and aroma families) under CC BY-SA 4.0.
      </li>
    </ul>

